1
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:06,137
The reason why it's there is?

2
00:01:06,220 --> 00:01:07,860
I will protect you!

3
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:12,817
Don't worry, let's go ahead!

4
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:16,460
The moon will always come to the moon.

5
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:19,097
The moon will come to the moon.

6
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:22,497
Let's look at the moon.

7
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:27,877
Let's look at the moon.

8
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:31,057
It will be a place to go to the future.

9
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:33,760
That's why I'll be the same path.

10
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:37,697
I'll give you a wish.

11
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:41,740
We are one of them.

12
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,477
We might not be traveling in style,?

13
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:03,617
but I gotta admit, this sure is handy.

14
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:06,017
I never thought riding a
fish would be so comfy.

15
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:07,620
Over here! Over here!

16
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:10,060
Hey, here it comes! No problem!

17
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:15,140
Oh, no! It's too high! Get ready!
Watch out! I got it! Oh, man!

18
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:16,670
Stupid!

19
00:02:16,753 --> 00:02:17,857
This is not your fault!

20
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:19,411
I was gonna get that one!

21
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:21,680
I want to play, too!

22
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:25,170
Ugh.

23
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:28,717
I didn't think there'd be canals
running by people's houses, too.

24
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:29,918
They're everywhere.

25
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:35,365
I'm trying to follow the map, but
I don't want to miss anything.

26
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:43,590
Huh?

27
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:47,738
Uh, we're about to go against
the flow, is that okay?

28
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:50,018
We're not supposed to go up, are we?

29
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:56,700
What's wrong way?

30
00:02:56,820 --> 00:02:57,761
Go right, right!

31
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,070
Awesome!

32
00:03:00,153 --> 00:03:02,060
You horsefish can swim uphill too?

33
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,960
What can't you do?

34
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:07,550
Look!

35
00:03:07,633 --> 00:03:10,560
The canals go to the top
of the building! Who cares?

36
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:12,569
We're going the wrong way!

37
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:15,600
We need to go to the
shopping district! Why?

38
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:16,801
What's the rush?

39
00:03:17,020 --> 00:03:19,726
You wanna see the rest
of the city, don't you?

40
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:25,680
Look, look! Do something! Turn around!

41
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:28,852
Oh yeah, we're up pretty high, aren't we?

42
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:31,000
That's not what I want to hear!

43
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:50,900
Help me!

44
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:09,120
Stop showing off!

45
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,390
Huh?

46
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:17,677
Best prices in town. Check us out.

47
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:19,120
Take a look over here.

48
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:20,577
I promise you won't regret it.

49
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:22,317
We're starting our 50 % off sale.

50
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,230
Don't miss it.

51
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:31,060
We've got rare goods for
the distinguished customer.

52
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:34,520
Oh, man, check out all the stuff.

53
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:37,497
We ended up in the shopping
district after all.

54
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:40,109
Wait, you guys took a
shortcut, didn't you?

55
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:42,900
I'm sorry.

56
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:45,177
You're a lot smarter than
I gave you credit for.

57
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:48,378
This has got to be the
biggest market I've ever seen!

58
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:49,610
Uh-huh.

59
00:04:49,693 --> 00:04:50,523
Whoa, look!

60
00:04:50,606 --> 00:04:53,780
That bull is huge! Whoa! Should we move?

61
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:55,488
It's coming straight at us!

62
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:03,200
That thing is scary!

63
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:04,739
Pinky eats people?

64
00:05:04,860 --> 00:05:06,684
I wonder if this one is a king.

65
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:08,490
Huh?

66
00:05:08,573 --> 00:05:09,403
What's with them?

67
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:11,109
They're all wearing masks!

68
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,377
Wow, neat. They're pretty.

69
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:16,225
They must be going to a party.

70
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:20,080
What's up? See something?

71
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:24,359
Freshly made water water
octopus dumplings for sale.

72
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:27,940
Three water water croquettes coming up.

73
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:29,806
I didn't know they sold food.

74
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:31,841
I'm hungry, let's buy everything!

75
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,520
Wait, go back!

76
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:36,622
Hey, Lopey, where are you going?

77
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:39,080
I don't know, ask my ride.

78
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:40,570
Huh?

79
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,600
Hello there.

80
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:48,480
How may I help you?

81
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,800
I see, so you were hungry, too.

82
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:54,197
Water-water meat is the
Yagara's favorite food,

83
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:56,377
although we usually cook it for humans.

84
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:57,290
Meat, huh?

85
00:05:57,373 --> 00:05:58,434
I'll take ten, please.

86
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:03,257
They're so good that the cooks from the
gourmet town come by them in secret.

87
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:05,693
Bet you never had anything like it, huh?

88
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:12,000
So soft! Yummy!

89
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:15,460
Oh, really? They're good?

90
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:16,960
Let me try one, Luffy.

91
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:19,100
No way, I'm not sharing.

92
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:21,880
Nami, he's being mean.

93
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:23,473
Make him share with me.

94
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:25,660
More masks.

95
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:28,175
People all over town are wearing them.

96
00:06:28,780 --> 00:06:30,956
There's something strange about this.

97
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:34,312
Nami, are you listening?

98
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,300
This is it.

99
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:40,417
As soon as we take the Watergate elevator,

100
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,206
will be at the Shipbuilding
Island in no time.

101
00:06:44,980 --> 00:06:46,920
What's this Watergate thing?

102
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:49,260
It's that tower right ahead of us.

103
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:57,500
Attention, everyone!

104
00:06:58,660 --> 00:07:00,860
The elevator is ready to go.

105
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:02,847
Bulls and riders, enter now.

106
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:05,295
Proceed in an orderly fashion, please.

107
00:07:05,620 --> 00:07:07,937
All aboard for Shipbuilding Island?

108
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:13,677
In downtown Water 7 at this time passengers
should enter the elevator quickly.

109
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:16,557
The gate will Be closing
in only one minute.

110
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:20,737
Something crazy is gonna happen!

111
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:21,702
I just know it!

112
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:29,277
The gate closed. It's starting!

113
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:38,460
I see.

114
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:40,620
First you go in, the gate shuts,

115
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:44,881
the water fills the elevator, and
then everybody floats to the top.

116
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:48,720
I still don't get it,
but it sure is awesome.

117
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:52,440
They really do use water
for everything here.

118
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:03,640
Hey Who are you calling moss head jerk?

119
00:08:04,340 --> 00:08:05,560
You awake?

120
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:08,960
Uh-huh You know where Robin went?

121
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:10,335
She's not on the ship

122
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:13,937
Oh, I remember.

123
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:17,740
She said she was going
out with Chopper! What?

124
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:20,395
They were doing some shopping, I think

125
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:21,590
What the hell?

126
00:08:21,673 --> 00:08:24,557
Does that mean I'm stuck on
this ship alone with you?

127
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:27,640
That's gotta be the most
boring thing in the world!

128
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:29,666
Yep, that's why I'm sleeping.

129
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:31,810
Fine.

130
00:08:31,893 --> 00:08:34,677
I need to do our grocery
shopping so I'm taking off too.

131
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:37,231
Take good care of the boat while I'm gone.

132
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,260
Sleep already, huh?

133
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:43,290
Whatever.

134
00:08:43,373 --> 00:08:44,300
Keep up the good work.

135
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:15,460
We made it!

136
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:23,177
So this is the best shipyard
in the whole world, huh?

137
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:25,848
It's even fancier than
the rest of the town.

138
00:09:31,460 --> 00:09:34,557
They've got a lot more ground to work
with than the residential district,

139
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:35,581
that's for sure.

140
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:41,740
Everything's huge! So cool!

141
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,856
Of course it's cool!

142
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,313
This place is the best!

143
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:57,012
Oh, there's a bunch of people over there.

144
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:59,437
Think something's going
on at the shipyard?

145
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:00,797
Let's go check it out!

146
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:01,840
Go, Yoggana!

147
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:03,520
Yeah! Whoa!

148
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:06,560
Whoa, did you see that?

149
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:07,930
Oh, my God.

150
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:11,980
Look, over there, it's Luchi!

151
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:13,740
He's so handsome!

152
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:16,297
Pauly's here today, too, right?

153
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:18,137
Who cares about those guys, huh?

154
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:19,980
Now, Lulu, that's a real man.

155
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:21,688
Just look at that mustache!

156
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:23,050
Whatever!

157
00:10:23,133 --> 00:10:25,061
Nobody's manlier than Tile Stone!

158
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:27,400
Hey, mister!

159
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:28,850
Hmm?

160
00:10:28,933 --> 00:10:30,800
What's this crowd about? Oh,

161
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:32,977
it was just some boneheaded pirates trying

162
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:35,477
to pick a fight with
the shipwrights again.

163
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:37,420
You know, happens all the time.

164
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:40,097
But our guys send them
packing like always.

165
00:10:40,180 --> 00:10:42,577
Those pirates will never
learn their lesson.

166
00:10:42,660 --> 00:10:43,719
Whoa, that's nuts!

167
00:10:43,980 --> 00:10:45,857
The shipwrights can beat up pirates?

168
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:47,740
Ah, you must be tourists, huh?

169
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:49,685
The shipwrights are, well, hm.

170
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,777
They're like celebrities to us.

171
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:54,737
In fact, you might say that
this crowd is their fan club.

172
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:57,408
We're always watching
the Gallylock company.

173
00:10:57,560 --> 00:11:00,160
They're strong, they're skilled,

174
00:11:00,820 --> 00:11:04,060
and they're the pride of
every citizen in Water 7.

175
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:11,000
Wow, I can't wait to meet them.

176
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:17,200
Hey, Luffy, let's hurry up and
get the gold traded in, okay?

177
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:19,337
This is fun, but it can wait till later.

178
00:11:19,420 --> 00:11:20,250
Come on!

179
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:36,357
It says that we're in the
Backstreet Shopping District.

180
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:39,616
Seems awfully crowded for a
Backstreet, if you ask me.

181
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:43,497
Kinda neat that they have
places to walk around, though.

182
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:46,157
They must have put a lot of
thought into the town's design.

183
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,070
Yeah.

184
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,471
What is that guy selling?

185
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:52,541
It looks creepy.

186
00:11:52,780 --> 00:11:54,420
It's just a mask shop.

187
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:58,897
I noticed a lot of people
around town wearing them,

188
00:11:58,980 --> 00:12:00,117
so they must buy them from there.

189
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,157
It's something you wear?

190
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,537
I thought that was their face.

191
00:12:02,620 --> 00:12:04,091
Wow, that's a big relief.

192
00:12:07,340 --> 00:12:10,837
It seems the people here take the
Sea Train to San Faldo Island,

193
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:13,357
where they hold a costume
carnival every day.

194
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:14,270
Huh?

195
00:12:14,353 --> 00:12:15,183
How do you know that?

196
00:12:15,266 --> 00:12:16,096
We just got here.

197
00:12:16,179 --> 00:12:18,669
The people walking by
are talking about it.

198
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:19,830
Whoa.

199
00:12:19,913 --> 00:12:22,018
And do you hear everything they say?

200
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:23,480
I can't help it.

201
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:26,340
Ever since I was young,

202
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:30,557
I've made it a habit to keep a
critical eye and ear on my environment.

203
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:31,470
Oh.

204
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:33,000
Wow, Robin.

205
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:34,180
That's cool.

206
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:40,130
Huh.

207
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:41,290
Doctor.

208
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:42,510
Hmm?

209
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:43,630
See that?

210
00:12:43,780 --> 00:12:45,337
I think we found your bookstore.

211
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:46,250
Really?

212
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:48,200
Can we go inside?

213
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,720
Of course, be my guest.

214
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Today is the best day ever!

215
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:08,300
Cape.

216
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:25,497
Hey!

217
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:27,080
What are you waiting for?

218
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:56,800
If I'm in my human form,

219
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,772
Um, maybe it'll be okay.

220
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:01,320
Huh? Why?

221
00:14:01,780 --> 00:14:03,300
What a funny mask.

222
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:04,676
What's your costume?

223
00:14:05,460 --> 00:14:09,160
Oh, uh, a human reindeer? Hmm.

224
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:12,891
Well, as long as you're having fun, right?

225
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:14,330
Hmm.

226
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:16,260
Oh, hey, wait.

227
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:23,400
Robin? Robin?

228
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:26,130
Hello?

229
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:28,130
Robin?

230
00:15:05,380 --> 00:15:08,674
Pity, I was hoping that we
could kill you in your sleep.

231
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:14,396
You bastards sure got a lot of nerve.

232
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:16,140
Who are you?

233
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:19,820
100 million berries!

234
00:15:20,160 --> 00:15:20,990
Let down, stupid!

235
00:15:21,073 --> 00:15:24,117
You want the whole city to know
how much cash we're lugging around?

236
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:26,397
You're really gonna give
us that much money, mister?

237
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:27,656
Play it cool, Luffy.

238
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:30,117
You gotta handle these
things like a professional.

239
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:33,117
It may sound like a lot, but that's
most certainly what it's worth.

240
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:35,553
It has historical value and high purity.

241
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:40,257
With a hundred million, we can make
the Mary even better than before.

242
00:15:40,340 --> 00:15:42,297
No kidding, and we'll
have plenty to spare.

243
00:15:42,380 --> 00:15:45,257
Then we'll spend the rest on a
big statue to put on the deck.

244
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:46,500
No, no, we won't.

245
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:47,517
Well, that's wonderful.

246
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:48,737
I'm glad you accept the amount.

247
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:51,277
Now I need your thumbprint
and signature here.

248
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:54,197
After that, I'll prepare
your money lickety-split.

249
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:56,537
You can have both my
thumbs if you want them!

250
00:15:56,620 --> 00:15:57,450
Mine too!

251
00:15:57,533 --> 00:15:59,419
The more thumbs, the better, right?

252
00:16:09,780 --> 00:16:10,840
Uh, what's up?

253
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,057
Giving him a tillprint?

254
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:15,905
Before we sign anything, there
are three things I'd like to say.

255
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:17,500
Mr. Appraiser.

256
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:23,860
First, I forgot to mention this, but he's
got a 100 million bounty on his head.

257
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:29,940
Second, I don't accept
the appraisal you gave us.

258
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:33,040
Third, if you try to lie to us again,

259
00:16:33,700 --> 00:16:36,960
it'll be the last lie you
ever tell. You got that?

260
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:40,380
Please forgive me!

261
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:43,300
300 million?

262
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:45,960
This is like a dream come true!

263
00:16:46,940 --> 00:16:50,257
Skypiea paid off after all, I
never thought I'd see the day.

264
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:52,417
You know, I always wanted
to be filthy, right?

265
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:53,618
It's our money too!

266
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:55,397
Pleasure doing business with you.

267
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:58,337
I'm so comfortable having all
this money in one place, guys.

268
00:16:58,420 --> 00:16:59,260
It's scary.

269
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:02,953
I mean, what if I trip and it
all falls out or something?

270
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:04,620
That was great.

271
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:07,036
You sure were scary back there, Nami.

272
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:11,677
I estimated 300 million from the start,
but I figured he wouldn't give it up easy.

273
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:13,717
He really got to work on your game face.

274
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:14,717
Good thing I was there.

275
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:15,630
Cut it out.

276
00:17:15,713 --> 00:17:18,166
You're making me nervous
swinging that around.

277
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:19,440
Well, whatever.

278
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:22,366
We got our money now,
and that's what matters.

279
00:17:24,740 --> 00:17:26,020
You dropped it!

280
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:28,365
Don't let it fall in the room!

281
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:35,275
Phew, that would've been bad
if the money got wet, huh?

282
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:38,897
If you lose my money,
you're playing and flying!

283
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:41,117
Keep out and cramming down your throat!

284
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,277
I'm sorry, very sorry.

285
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:46,220
But please, don't break my face anymore.

286
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:02,000
You don't know who we are? Really?

287
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:05,073
Because we sure know you, Pirate Hunter.

288
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:10,217
Babies stop crying when
they hear our name.

289
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:12,124
A collection of bounty hunters!

290
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:15,220
We are the Franky family!

291
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:17,477
Now if you don't mind,

292
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:20,897
I think we'll be taking that 60
million bounty you've got on your head.

293
00:18:20,980 --> 00:18:22,217
When we're done with you,

294
00:18:22,300 --> 00:18:23,977
we'll wait inside that cabin of yours and

295
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:26,884
ambush the rest of your
crew when they get back.

296
00:18:28,580 --> 00:18:31,345
We're gonna be rolling
in the dough in no time!

297
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:33,840
It's my lucky day!

298
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:37,910
Lucky, huh?

299
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:43,460
We'll see about that now, won't we? Ah!

300
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:54,100
Two swords, Tile!

301
00:18:55,500 --> 00:18:56,460
Rhino!

302
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:57,660
Psycho!

303
00:19:08,140 --> 00:19:10,400
Back to sleep.

304
00:19:13,580 --> 00:19:14,410
Oh, man!

305
00:19:17,620 --> 00:19:18,940
I don't know, Nami.

306
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:21,917
Maybe we should take the cash
back to the ship after all.

307
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,897
That'd be a complete waste of time.

308
00:19:23,980 --> 00:19:25,797
The shipyard is right around the corner.

309
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:28,457
Come on, you don't have
to ride so far away.

310
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:29,937
Let me play with the money.

311
00:19:30,020 --> 00:19:32,897
Anyway, we'll probably head
back to the Mary soon enough.

312
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:35,877
After we meet with the shipwrights, I'm
sure they'll need to look at the damages?

313
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:37,477
before they can give us a quote.

314
00:19:37,560 --> 00:19:38,957
I didn't think of it that way.

315
00:19:39,040 --> 00:19:40,677
I guess I could watch the money till then.

316
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:43,417
I've never carried so much
cash at once, that's all.

317
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:44,817
I don't know how to handle it.

318
00:19:44,900 --> 00:19:46,429
Well, that's only natural.

319
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:49,857
Just don't flail it around and throw
it in any rivers and you'll be fine.

320
00:19:49,940 --> 00:19:52,037
Ooh, they're selling
water buns over there.

321
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:53,277
Let's buy a hundred of them.

322
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:54,190
Shut up.

323
00:19:54,273 --> 00:19:55,103
How about a thousand?

324
00:19:55,186 --> 00:19:56,016
Shut up.

325
00:19:56,099 --> 00:19:56,929
Shut up.

326
00:19:57,012 --> 00:19:57,842
How about shut up?

327
00:19:57,925 --> 00:19:58,755
Okay.

328
00:20:11,880 --> 00:20:13,527
Right, back to the shipyard.

329
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:16,405
And it looks like the
crowd's cleared out, too.

330
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:18,717
Well, that's good.

331
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:22,537
We have enough to deal with without the
Shipwright fan club getting in the way.

332
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:24,737
All we gotta do is find that ice guy.

333
00:20:24,820 --> 00:20:27,440
Uh, wait, what's his name again?

334
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:28,950
It's Iceberg.

335
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:31,340
Oh, yeah, now I remember Ice Pops.

336
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:34,477
The old lady back at the train station
said that's who we needed to talk to,

337
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:37,337
but now that I think about it, we
don't know anything about him, do we?

338
00:20:37,420 --> 00:20:38,757
Well, it's the only lead we've got.

339
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:40,337
I don't even know how this place works.

340
00:20:40,420 --> 00:20:42,008
Is it okay just to walk in?

341
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:45,080
That's what I'm doing! Not again!

342
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:48,080
Hold it right there.

343
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:52,078
You got a lot of gumption
just waltzing in like that.

344
00:20:52,380 --> 00:20:55,498
Why don't we take a step
over here, then we can talk.

345
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:58,424
Don't worry, it's not personal.

346
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:02,325
You're outsiders is all, so you're
not allowed inside the plant.

347
00:21:04,040 --> 00:21:05,020
Oopsy-daisy.

348
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:11,837
All right, Champ, what brings
you to the docks today?

349
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:13,744
Come on, Usopp, I know it's you

350
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:16,420
I'm right here, Loopy! Idiot!

351
00:21:16,700 --> 00:21:19,377
Oh, now that I look at
it, his nose is square.

352
00:21:19,460 --> 00:21:23,457
Anyway, that aside, we came here to
see Iceberg, if that's all right?

353
00:21:23,540 --> 00:21:25,177
Hmm, is that so, little miss?

354
00:21:25,260 --> 00:21:26,319
Are you customers?

355
00:21:26,820 --> 00:21:27,817
Oh, that's nifty.

356
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:30,137
Not every day that
youngsters come here with

357
00:21:30,220 --> 00:21:32,097
a letter of introduction
from Granny Kokoro!

358
00:21:32,180 --> 00:21:36,660
Uh, hold on, how old are
you? I'm 23. Why do you ask?

359
00:21:36,780 --> 00:21:39,057
You know, for someone who's
hardly any older than us,

360
00:21:39,140 --> 00:21:41,081
you sure do talk like an old man.

361
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:42,900
I get that a lot.

362
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:46,057
So do you know Iceberg, or do
we come to the wrong place?

363
00:21:46,140 --> 00:21:47,837
Well, of course I know Iceberg.

364
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:49,857
Why, I'd say that everyone here knows him,

365
00:21:49,940 --> 00:21:52,587
seeing as he's the mayor
of the city and all.

366
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:54,410
Wow.

367
00:21:54,493 --> 00:21:55,940
Ice Pops is an important guy, huh?

368
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:57,540
Darn Skippy he is.

369
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:59,477
He's also the president of our galley law

370
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:02,257
company and manager of the
C-train on top of that.

371
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:03,757
I didn't know he was such a big deal.

372
00:22:03,840 --> 00:22:06,257
I had a feeling you
weren't from around here.

373
00:22:06,340 --> 00:22:08,317
Iceberg is pretty famous in these parts.

374
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:09,897
But do you know where we can find him?

375
00:22:09,980 --> 00:22:12,039
Hmm, that's the question, isn't it?

376
00:22:12,780 --> 00:22:14,662
He keeps pretty busy, of course.

377
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:17,057
Hunting him down can be a chore sometimes.

378
00:22:17,140 --> 00:22:18,787
But you work for him, right?

379
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:20,477
Can't you get in touch somehow?

380
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:23,637
I suppose I could, but it seems like
you're in a hurry to get this done.

381
00:22:23,720 --> 00:22:25,320
Not exactly, but...

382
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:28,020
It's fine, I understand.

383
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:31,781
You're richin' to have
your ship looked at, right?

384
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:33,412
Where did you anchor it?

385
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:35,722
Uh, it's over by the rocky cape.

386
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:38,557
Alrighty then, I'll skedaddle
over there real quick.

387
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:40,797
If I take a gander at
your ship beforehand,

388
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:43,097
you can start talking cost
with Iceberg right away.

389
00:22:43,180 --> 00:22:46,977
As I said, he's very busy, so I'm
sure he'll be grateful as well.

390
00:22:47,060 --> 00:22:48,660
Wait, skedaddle like how?

391
00:22:49,040 --> 00:22:50,380
On a yagata or what?

392
00:22:51,500 --> 00:22:53,735
I thought we were trying to save time.

393
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:56,337
If you folks can hang
tight for 10 minutes,

394
00:22:56,420 --> 00:22:58,617
I should be back in two
shakes of a lamb's tail.

395
00:22:58,700 --> 00:22:59,641
Just 10 minutes?

396
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,820
That's right, or your money back.

397
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:06,900
Whoa!

398
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:10,860
He's fast!

399
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:16,070
Whoa!

400
00:23:16,153 --> 00:23:17,200
He flew!

401
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:21,360
Wait, where's he going?

402
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:23,896
If he jumps off the edge, he'll fall!

403
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:26,160
Whoa! Come back!

404
00:23:35,460 --> 00:23:38,817
So cool yeah but is he gonna be okay?

405
00:23:38,900 --> 00:23:43,037
Don't worry he's always
soaring through town!

406
00:23:43,120 --> 00:23:49,177
Huh they call him the mountain
wind if you didn't know

407
00:23:49,260 --> 00:23:55,440
he's the galley law company's
doc one carpentry foreman kaku

408
00:23:59,800 --> 00:24:00,640
I see.

409
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:02,920
So this is the city of water, huh?

410
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:05,252
Pretty impressive place.

411
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:07,157
Lives up to its name, that's for sure.

412
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:08,580
I mean, look around.

413
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:13,497
Clean water, clean streets, fresh food,
and most importantly, plenty of cute girls.

414
00:24:13,580 --> 00:24:14,874
This place has it all.

415
00:24:15,140 --> 00:24:16,417
Take my word for it,

416
00:24:16,500 --> 00:24:20,697
this is the perfect place to take that
special someone on a romantic stroll.

417
00:24:20,780 --> 00:24:23,721
But why stop at one when
I have two lovely ladies?

418
00:24:26,180 --> 00:24:28,920
This one is Nami, and
this one here is Robin.

419
00:24:29,660 --> 00:24:31,660
You're scaring away the customers.

420
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:35,937
Stop making that creepy face and tell me
which water water cabbage you want already.

421
00:24:36,020 --> 00:24:37,373
I'll take both of them.

422
00:24:37,460 --> 00:24:39,237
Oh, and there was something
I wanted to ask you.

423
00:24:39,320 --> 00:24:42,097
I'm looking for some local specialties
that are in season right now.

424
00:24:42,180 --> 00:24:44,380
So what have you got? Let's see.

425
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:45,990
This way?

426
00:24:47,320 --> 00:24:50,144
This place sure is a pain
when you have to walk.

427
00:24:52,460 --> 00:24:56,397
If I don't stop running into dead ends and
start figuring out where the hell I am,

428
00:24:56,480 --> 00:24:59,097
this food's going to go bad
before I make it back to the Mary.

429
00:24:59,180 --> 00:25:03,121
Don't tell me Zorro's brain fungus
is starting to spread to me too.

430
00:25:10,420 --> 00:25:12,560
Robin, boy, am I glad to see you!

431
00:25:12,820 --> 00:25:14,660
It's me, Sanji! Yoo-hoo!

432
00:25:16,120 --> 00:25:17,360
Robin, look!

433
00:25:22,080 --> 00:25:23,021
She disappeared.

434
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:25,600
Looks like another dead end to me.

435
00:25:26,860 --> 00:25:29,460
The only way to go is up, but there's...

436
00:25:33,380 --> 00:25:34,210
Usopp?

437
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:37,468
Man, I don't know what's
up with this place.

438
00:25:38,080 --> 00:25:39,980
I'm not going crazy, am I?

439
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:54,160
Well, Lock here.

440
00:25:54,420 --> 00:25:55,655
That must be the one.

441
00:25:59,620 --> 00:26:00,450
Pardon me.

442
00:26:04,080 --> 00:26:05,780
Well, it's just your sub.

443
00:26:06,740 --> 00:26:07,620
My goodness.

444
00:26:07,920 --> 00:26:09,677
I know they told me their
ship needed repairs,

445
00:26:09,760 --> 00:26:12,289
but I didn't think it
would be in shambles.

446
00:26:14,820 --> 00:26:17,240
We should start by replacing this mast.

447
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:22,100
Wait, that's not right.

448
00:26:22,500 --> 00:26:25,440
Hey, I see you! Don't move! You hear me?

449
00:26:25,660 --> 00:26:26,680
Oh, pardon.

450
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:28,797
I didn't intend to disturb your nap.

451
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:31,040
Jeez, that was a big surprise.

452
00:26:31,320 --> 00:26:33,967
I've never seen someone
jump that far before.

453
00:26:34,280 --> 00:26:37,717
Well, my craftsmen are the best
in the business for a reason.

454
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:39,680
Who is this guy? Don't ask me.

455
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:42,897
Extraordinary ships are not born
from ordinary circumstances.

456
00:26:42,980 --> 00:26:45,804
They require a nearly
superhuman level of skill.

457
00:26:46,540 --> 00:26:48,037
By the way, Clover...

458
00:26:48,120 --> 00:26:49,837
I've already finished
the background check.

459
00:26:49,920 --> 00:26:51,957
The one in the middle is Straw Hat Luffy.

460
00:26:52,040 --> 00:26:55,452
His crew also includes Pirate
Hunter Zoro and Nico Robin.

461
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:58,920
Their combined bounty is 239 million.

462
00:26:59,180 --> 00:27:01,477
They have four other members
without posted bounties,

463
00:27:01,560 --> 00:27:04,089
and their crew was
formed in the East Blue.

464
00:27:04,280 --> 00:27:07,857
Named after their captain, they're
known simply as the Straw Hat Pirates.

465
00:27:07,940 --> 00:27:11,140
They've really got our
number! I see. Welcome.

466
00:27:11,440 --> 00:27:12,680
My name is Iceberg.

467
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:13,939
I'm the boss here.

468
00:27:14,400 --> 00:27:16,580
And this is a mouse I just picked up.

469
00:27:17,680 --> 00:27:20,580
Its name is, let's see, Tyrannosaurus.

470
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:23,497
I'll need some rodent food in a cage.

471
00:27:23,580 --> 00:27:25,617
I've already taken care of that, sir.

472
00:27:25,700 --> 00:27:27,557
Well, amazing work, Carly Fire.

473
00:27:27,640 --> 00:27:28,720
Just doing my job.

474
00:27:29,460 --> 00:27:30,519
Speaking of which,

475
00:27:30,680 --> 00:27:34,697
you're due at a hotel in Chess for lunch
with a glassware factory executive.

476
00:27:34,780 --> 00:27:37,357
After that, you're set to make
a speech at Liguria Square.

477
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:39,757
And once that's finished,
you'll be meeting with Mr.

478
00:27:39,840 --> 00:27:41,077
Bimini, the mayor of Pucci.

479
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:44,557
Their local newspaper is scheduled
to interview you as well.

480
00:27:44,640 --> 00:27:48,197
Oh, and when you return to the office,
there's a folder full of important documents?

481
00:27:48,280 --> 00:27:49,751
I need your signature on.

482
00:27:50,080 --> 00:27:51,080
I don't wanna.

483
00:27:52,500 --> 00:27:55,077
Very well, then I'll
cancel everything for you.

484
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:57,077
Hold on, you're not serious, are you?

485
00:27:57,160 --> 00:28:00,177
What's the point of having power
if I don't get to do what I want?

486
00:28:00,260 --> 00:28:03,457
If that's how you run things, you
gotta be the worst mayor in the world.

487
00:28:03,540 --> 00:28:05,217
Yeah, Pops, that's pretty lazy.

488
00:28:05,300 --> 00:28:08,757
So, hold on, are you sure this is the
guy that old lady was talking about?

489
00:28:08,840 --> 00:28:10,722
Uh-huh, he's the guy, all right.

490
00:28:11,160 --> 00:28:12,040
How dare you!

491
00:28:19,180 --> 00:28:20,800
What's the big idea, lady?

492
00:28:20,980 --> 00:28:21,862
That was scary.

493
00:28:28,220 --> 00:28:30,797
I won't stand here and
let you insolent louts

494
00:28:30,880 --> 00:28:33,677
disrespect one of the world's
leading ship engineers.

495
00:28:33,760 --> 00:28:35,017
Hey, what's going on over there?

496
00:28:35,100 --> 00:28:37,637
Iceberg's secretary just flipped
out on some pirates again.

497
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:38,837
I wish she'd flip out on me.

498
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:39,880
Pardon me.

499
00:28:40,220 --> 00:28:42,557
I get a bit carried
away from time to time.

500
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:47,137
Still, Iceberg is a respected figure here
in Water 7, so try to show some courtesy.

501
00:28:47,220 --> 00:28:49,220
Yes, please don't provoke Kalifa.

502
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:53,160
When she lashes out in
anger, her brain sucks.

503
00:28:54,680 --> 00:28:57,237
We might have hurt his
feelings, but you hurt his face!

504
00:28:57,320 --> 00:28:58,849
You're way meaner than us!

505
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:02,657
Putting all that behind us, if you're
Iceberg, you're the man we're looking for.

506
00:29:02,740 --> 00:29:05,517
Here, we brought a letter of
introduction for you to look at.

507
00:29:05,600 --> 00:29:06,740
From Granny Kokoro?

508
00:29:08,140 --> 00:29:10,434
Oh, take a look at their ship, it says.

509
00:29:12,260 --> 00:29:13,680
What? Are you serious?

510
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:16,457
There has to be something we
can do to change your mind.

511
00:29:16,540 --> 00:29:18,297
If money's the issue, we can pay.

512
00:29:18,380 --> 00:29:21,417
If you're really the best, then you've
got to be the one to fix our Mary.

513
00:29:21,500 --> 00:29:22,677
Come on, we're begging.

514
00:29:22,760 --> 00:29:24,020
Okay. That's it?

515
00:29:24,220 --> 00:29:25,497
You don't need to think about it?

516
00:29:25,580 --> 00:29:26,410
Nope.

517
00:29:26,493 --> 00:29:27,597
Hey, why did you tear up the letter?

518
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:29,497
The lipstick mark was creeping me out.

519
00:29:29,580 --> 00:29:32,597
Even so, Granny Kokoro and I have
been drinking buddies for years.

520
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:33,510
Well,

521
00:29:33,593 --> 00:29:35,437
and since Kaku has already gone
to make an assessment for me,

522
00:29:35,520 --> 00:29:37,677
it would seem like a waste
to turn you down now,

523
00:29:37,760 --> 00:29:38,760
wouldn't you say?

524
00:29:40,500 --> 00:29:42,697
Besides, it's not like I
had anything better to do.

525
00:29:42,780 --> 00:29:44,197
Let me show you around the factory.

526
00:29:44,280 --> 00:29:45,110
Sound good?

527
00:29:45,193 --> 00:29:46,060
Sweet! Bring it on!

528
00:29:46,340 --> 00:29:47,397
Come along with me, then.

529
00:29:47,480 --> 00:29:50,717
Did he seriously cancel all of his
meetings just to give us a tour?

530
00:29:50,800 --> 00:29:51,630
Yeah!

531
00:29:51,713 --> 00:29:53,782
You gotta let me sit on
all the cool ships, okay?

532
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:55,620
Oh, right. The money.

533
00:29:56,720 --> 00:29:58,220
Wait, what? No!

534
00:30:04,380 --> 00:30:05,851
Hey, what's wrong, Usopp?

535
00:30:05,960 --> 00:30:06,790
Come on.

536
00:30:07,840 --> 00:30:10,040
The money, it disappeared.

537
00:30:11,620 --> 00:30:13,180
Did she drop it somewhere?

538
00:30:13,540 --> 00:30:14,540
I don't know.

539
00:30:18,700 --> 00:30:20,280
Hey, over there!

540
00:30:27,680 --> 00:30:29,537
Wait who are you?

541
00:30:29,620 --> 00:30:31,037
Why are you taking your money?

542
00:30:31,120 --> 00:30:32,657
I mean, give it back.

543
00:30:32,740 --> 00:30:34,377
We need it. You jerks!

544
00:30:34,460 --> 00:30:35,457
Do you hear me?

545
00:30:35,540 --> 00:30:39,737
Thanks for the cash!

546
00:30:39,820 --> 00:30:42,360
Give us our money back!
